# Drops the release-time refresh of drag.pts against the touchend/pointerup's
# own e.timeStamp: velocity is computed straight from whatever pointermove
# aging left behind, with no fresh point and no re-prune at release. A flick
# followed by holding still (no further pointermove fires on a zero-delta
# touch move) leaves the initial fast segment sitting in drag.pts unaged, so
# a stale flick still reads as a fling instead of correctly aging out.
